0. Application and licensing history

This agreement applies only to versions of Make It Work expressly released by
Licensor under this agreement (the Software). Public availability of source code
does not make those versions open-source licensed. Approval of these terms does
not itself publish a commercial version, relicense previously published code,
or start a trial for existing users. Prior grants remain governed by their
original terms; see section 8 and the archived texts in docs/licensing/.

An individual accepting for an organization represents that they are authorized
to bind it. The organization accepting these terms is Customer. Before the
first installation or execution of a commercially licensed version, an
authorized individual must review and accept these terms on Customer's behalf.
The terms must be presented in the installation instructions before
installation commands. A written order accepted by both parties (Order Form)
identifies Customer, fees, currency, payment due date, subscription start and
end dates, and any expressly included affiliates or additional terms. For a
paid subscription, the Order Form or a separate written agreement must also
specify the agreed governing law and court jurisdiction.

1. Free trial

The trial is self-service. No registration, email approval, credit card, or
payment is required to start it. Customer is responsible for recording its
organization's earliest installation or execution date and complying with the
30-day limit. This agreement does not require or represent that the Software
technically tracks or enforces the trial.

Customer may evaluate the Software for its internal business operations for one
30-day evaluation period per organization, beginning at its first installation
or execution of a commercially licensed version, whichever occurs first. The
trial includes use by Customer's employees and authorized contractors solely on
Customer's behalf, and internal modifications for that evaluation.
Reinstalling, upgrading, using a different developer account or machine, or
removing trial records does not restart or extend the trial. Use of an earlier
version under a prior license does not itself trigger this trial.

After 30 days, continued use of commercially licensed versions requires an
active paid annual subscription. Without one, Customer must stop using those
versions and remove operational copies, including internal modifications.
Customer may retain an inaccessible archival copy solely as required by law,
not for execution or further use. Customer's own artifacts and prior-license
rights are unaffected. The trial carries no payment obligation unless Customer
separately orders a subscription; it does not automatically convert to paid
use.

2. Annual organization license

Subject to payment and compliance, Licensor grants Customer a nonexclusive,
nontransferable license for a 12-month subscription term to install, execute,
copy internally, and internally modify the Software for Customer's internal
business operations. Unlimited employees and authorized contractors may use it
solely on Customer's behalf, across unlimited internal repositories and
installations. Contractors receive no independent license and must be bound by
restrictions at least as protective as these terms; Customer is responsible for
their use. Internal access by these authorized users is permitted and is not
prohibited redistribution or sublicensing.

Customer means the single legal organization named in the Order Form. Parent
companies, subsidiaries, and other affiliates are excluded unless expressly
included in that Order Form. No seat-based or repository-based limit applies
within the licensed organization. Continued use after the 12-month term
requires renewal; the license is not perpetual, including for copies downloaded
or modified while subscribed. Customer may use and deliver its own work
products, including commercial products, as described in section 5.

3. Restrictions and public hosting

Except for authorized internal access above or express written permission from
Licensor, Customer must not redistribute, resell, sublicense, rent, lend, or
transfer the Software or its modifications, or offer the plugin itself as a
hosted commercial service. Customer must preserve applicable copyright,
license, and third-party notices and must not misrepresent ownership or remove
notices from internal copies. No trademark rights are granted.

These restrictions do not limit rights required by applicable law, rights under
prior licenses, or independent third-party licenses. They do not restrict
GitHub's or its users' rights to host, view, and fork the public repository
through GitHub functionality under applicable GitHub terms. Such hosting rights
do not independently grant a right to execute commercially licensed versions
outside these terms or to redistribute them outside those platform rights.

4. Fees, payment, and renewal

To purchase an annual organization license, Customer contacts
insideoutaitech@gmail.com. Customer and Licensor agree to a quote or Order Form
identifying the licensed organization, annual fee, currency, payment method,
subscription start and end dates, and applicable legal terms. The annual fee is
payable in full upfront, before the paid subscription begins. After receiving
payment, Licensor confirms the 12-month organization license and its agreed
start and end dates in writing. A paid term starts only after payment and
written confirmation; agreed dates must not authorize unpaid use. An unpaid
purchase or renewal does not start or extend a paid term. There is no automatic
payment grace period or right to continue using commercial versions after the
trial or paid term expires. The trial does not require this purchase process.
No online checkout, activation key, or payment platform is required by these
terms.

Fees, currency, taxes, payment method, and due dates are specified in the Order
Form; this agreement sets no price. Customer pays applicable transaction taxes
other than taxes on Licensor's income. Fees are nonrefundable for a change of
mind, non-use, or voluntary cancellation, except for the unused-period refund
under section 9, any refund separately agreed in writing, or refunds required
by law. The 30-day remedy period for other material breaches in section 9 does
not provide a payment grace period or extend trial or subscription rights.

Subscriptions renew manually; there is no automatic renewal or automatic
billing. To renew, Customer and Licensor agree to a new annual quote or Order
Form, Customer pays the renewal fee in full upfront, and Licensor confirms the
renewed 12-month license and agreed dates in writing. Licensor will disclose
proposed renewal fees before Customer agrees to renew. Customer must complete
renewal before the current term expires for uninterrupted use. A renewal begins
on the agreed date and lasts 12 months. A gap in subscription provides no right
to use commercially licensed versions during that gap. Expiration or nonrenewal
has the same cessation and removal obligations as trial expiration, and ends
access to subscription maintenance. Customer's own artifacts and rights under
previously published licenses remain unaffected.

