9. Termination

Either party may terminate for the other's material breach if not cured within
30 days after written notice describing the breach. This notice-and-cure period
does not extend an expired trial or subscription or authorize use beyond an
active license term. Customer may discontinue use at any time; doing so does
not excuse accrued payment obligations. Trial and subscription rights also
expire at their stated end without notice. Upon expiration or termination,
Customer must stop using the applicable commercially licensed Software and
remove operational copies and modifications, subject to the legally required
archival exception in section 1. Accrued payment duties, ownership,
restrictions, disclaimers, liability limits, dispute provisions, and
prior-license protections survive as relevant. Customer's own artifacts remain
Customer's property and may continue to be used under section 5.

If Customer terminates because of Licensor's material breach that remains
uncured after the 30-day written-notice period above, Licensor will refund the
unused portion of prepaid subscription fees, prorated from the effective date
of termination through the end of the prepaid subscription term. This refund is
not available for a change of mind, non-use, or voluntary cancellation. Refunds
required by law or separately agreed in writing remain available.

