TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, NEITHER PARTY IS LIABLE TO THE OTHER
FOR INDIRECT OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES, OR LOST PROFITS OR REVENUE ARISING UNDER
THIS AGREEMENT. Other direct damages remain subject to the applicable liability
rules above and below.

For paid subscriptions, each party's aggregate liability under this agreement
is limited to the fees paid or payable under it for the 12 months preceding the
event giving rise to the claim. Ordinary, unintentional contractual errors
remain subject to this cap where applicable.

Neither the exclusions nor the cap in this section excuses Customer's
obligation to pay agreed fees or limits liability for fraud, deliberate
misconduct, or deliberate misuse of the other party's intellectual property,
including deliberate unauthorized resale or redistribution of the Software.
Neither the exclusions nor the cap limits liability that applicable law does
